  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1206 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nAfter a very cold morning, temperatures on Monday will only warm to \nthe upper 40s for much of the forecast area. Colder temperatures \nwith highs in the 40s and lows at or below freezing are expected to \nprevail everyday through Thursday before a potential \"warm up\" to \nthe 50s by this weekend. The coldest morning looks be Wednesday with \nlows below 30 degrees across the forecast area. The rest of the day \nMonday is expected to be quiet with light east to southeasterly \nwinds, however the main show will be overnight Monday into Tuesday. \nAn upper trough will translate across western CONUS to start off the \nweek before reaching the Texas Panhandle late Monday. Plenty of \nmoisture and the passage of this upper system will bring potential \nfor rain and snow showers overnight Monday through Tuesday morning. \nAt the moment, confidence on what type of precipitation that will \noccur is low. If snow is able to fall, accumulation is not expected \nwith how fast the system is expected to exit to the east. The rest \nof the week will be cold, however conditions will be dry. Previous \nforecast runs had potential for more rain and snow showers this \nupcoming weekend with the approach of another upper system. However, \ncurrent model runs are in disagreement with the upper pattern for \nthe latter half of the week, therefore NBM has backed off on \nprecipitation chances completely. Can expect precipitation chances \nfor the latter half of the week to continue to oscillate for future \nforecasts until models come to a better agreement.",
